  "type": "elizaosDailySummary",
  "title": "Daily Report - 2026-08-08",
  "categories": {
    "title": "ElizaOS Token Declared Dead: Community Reacts to Shaw's Announcement",
    "content": [
      {
        "text": "In early August 2026, Shaw (founder of ElizaOS) publicly stated that the associated token is dead, the foundation is winding down, and there will be no further buybacks, supply support, or official token-related efforts. This followed a class-action lawsuit settlement that depleted remaining resources. Shaw acknowledged that many people lost money and expressed a desire to change that outcome, while also noting that the open-source AI agent software development is expected to continue without a linked token. Shaw reflected on past exploitation, stating that engineers and others who joined the project leveraged its value and his name for personal gain, and that the bear market period is now focused on building with a small, focused team and no token involvement.",
        "sources": [
          "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241",
          "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1301363808421543988"
        ],
        "posters": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/posters/1786236430886-acphr4.jpg"
      },
      {
        "text": "Community members expressed frustration and a desire for clarity. Several holders who migrated from ai16z and held through account bans called on Shaw to formally remove token-related links from official ElizaOS channels and documentation to provide closure. Some users criticized the pattern of rebranding followed by abandonment, with token holders feeling left without recourse. At least one community member stated they would consult a lawyer regarding significant financial losses. Others questioned whether the GitHub repository would be archived or abandoned entirely, while Shaw clarified that the software project itself continues. A supporter noted that Shaw had been used by many people throughout the project's history and expressed optimism about a redemption arc going forward.",
        "sources": [
          "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241",
          "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1301363808421543988"
        ],
        "videos": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/elizaos-media/lv_0_20251104003508_2912fa08.mp4",
        "posters": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/posters/1786236457609-gc49z.jpg"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the coders channel, Shaw advised that for any agent project to succeed, the agent itself must demonstrate the ability to generate revenue. He also cautioned that if outside investors are brought in, the project should not be closed off from open-source principles.",
        "sources": "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1300025221834739744",
        "posters": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/posters/1786236482075-g5jbl.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "topic": "discordrawdata"
  },
